---
import GenericPageLayout from '../../layouts/GenericPageLayout.astro';
import styles from '../../styles/about.module.css';
---

<GenericPageLayout 
  title="Clubs & Societies" 
  subtitle="Extracurricular engagement and networking."
  heroImage="/media/DSC_3856.webp"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Campus', href: '/campus' },
    { label: 'Clubs', href: '/campus/clubs' }
  ]}
>
  <div class={styles.contentWrapper}>
    <h2 class={styles.heading2}>Beyond the Classroom</h2>
    <p class={styles.paragraph}>
      FUAZ strongly encourages students to participate in registered clubs and societies. These groups foster leadership skills, professional networking, and deep, lasting friendships outside of the grueling academic timetables.
    </p>

    <h2 class={styles.heading2}>Prominent Associations</h2>
    <ul class={styles.list}>
      <li><strong>Departmental Associations:</strong> e.g., Nigerian Association of Agricultural Students (NAAS), Veterinary Medical Students Association (VUMSA).</li>
      <li><strong>Enactus FUAZ:</strong> A global community of student leaders committed to using entrepreneurial action to transform lives.</li>
      <li><strong>The Debate & Literary Club:</strong> Organizes inter-college public speaking tournaments and poetry slams.</li>
      <li><strong>Amnesty International (Campus Chapter):</strong> Focuses on human rights advocacy.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class={styles.importantBox}>
      <strong>Registration:</strong> All clubs must be officially registered with the Dean of Students' Affairs (DSA). Unregistered associations holding meetings on campus will face disciplinary action.
    </div>
  </div>
</GenericPageLayout>
